From 3223a467d3d52491c7f60c78c01ae9b4d2b41848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Currie <rob@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:17:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools: no ROOT-to-xrdroot timing comparison, only xrdroot's
 own wall times

The tutorial harness measured every tutorial against ROOT and kept the ratios
in a committed `baseline-timings.json`, with `--previous` to compare a run's
ratios against it. That measurement is retired: the aim is to be faster than
ROOT ultimately, so a ratio is a target that moves whenever either side does,
and it invites the wrong one.

So `tools/tutorials/timing.py` and `baseline-timings.json` go, with the
`-timings.json` snapshot `baseline` used to write beside the status baseline.
The reports keep a single column, xrdroot's own seconds, and rank the slowest
30 by it - that is the list speed work needs. The results' schema is bumped to
`xrdroot-tutorials/2` so an old results.json, whose `timings` block holds ROOT
seconds and ratios, is refused rather than redrawn.

Each run's own wall time stays in its record and in the progress line (ROOT's
and xrdroot's alike): that is a fact of the run and what the timeout is judged
on. The correctness comparison of stdout, files and images is untouched.

The ROOT-relative figures in AGENTS.md, docs/root.md, TODO.md and the 2026-11
state assessment go with it; W0-6, the ratio ratchet they described, is
dropped rather than re-aimed at xrdroot-only seconds.
